"""
## Purpose and audience
For compiler engineers verifying the `CompilerServices` typed-port container
(Feature 2: Pipeline Stage Ports). This is a system-level test: it wires the
default (noop) implementation of every pipeline-stage port — lexer, parser,
desugarer, type checker, HIR/MIR lowerers, backend, logger, module loader —
and drives a realistic end-to-end compilation scenario across all nine stage
boundaries, so a future stage-boundary contract change surfaces here first.
## Operator workflow
Run `./src/compiler_rust/target/bootstrap/simple run
test/03_system/compiler/compiler_services_system_spec.spl` after changing
`src/compiler/00.common/compiler_services.spl` or any noop port
implementation it defines.
## Compatibility and limitations
Every port here is the NOOP default (`create_default_services()`); this spec
proves the container wiring and stage-boundary contract, not a real lexer,
parser, or backend's behavior. A noop function returning an empty list or the
unchanged input is the documented contract, not a placeholder bug.
## Verification guidance and troubleshooting
A failure names the port and field whose noop behavior changed. Re-run after
editing any `_noop_*` function or `*Port` struct in `compiler_services.spl`.
"""
